{"content":[{"c":["GATH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Walled city (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.26.6","r":"2Chr.26.6","rawR":"2Chr.26.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.26.6","value":"2Chr.26.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 26:6"},") and one of the five chief cities of the Philistines, which also included Gaza, Ashdod, Ashkelon, and Ekron (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.3","r":"Josh.13.3","rawR":"Josh.13.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.3","value":"Josh.13.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.6.17","r":"1Sam.6.17","rawR":"1Sam.6.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.6.17","value":"1Sam.6.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 6:17"},"), all situated on or near the southern coast of Palestine. Although frequently involved in conflict with the Israelites, the city was apparently not subdued until David’s time (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.18.1","r":"1Chr.18.1","rawR":"1Chr.18.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.18.1","value":"1Chr.18.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 18:1"},"). It was a Canaanite city, the home of the giant Goliath (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.17.4","r":"1Sam.17.4","rawR":"1Sam.17.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.17.4","value":"1Sam.17.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 17:4"},") and other men of great height (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.18-22","r":"2Sam.21.18-22","rawR":"2Sam.21.18-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.18-22","value":"2Sam.21.18-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 21:18-22"},"). A remnant of the Anakim was left, even after the extensive campaigns of Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.10.36-39","r":"Josh.10.36-39","rawR":"Josh.10.36-39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.10.36-39","value":"Josh.10.36-39"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 10:36-39"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.21-22","r":"Josh.11.21-22","rawR":"Josh.11.21-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.21-22","value":"Josh.11.21-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:21-22"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["When the Philistines captured the ark of God, they carried it from Ebenezer to Ashdod, from there to Gath (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.5.8","r":"1Sam.5.8","rawR":"1Sam.5.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.5.8","value":"1Sam.5.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 5:8"},"), and then to Ekron. After many of the Philistines died or were stricken with tumors, the ark was returned to Israel, first to Beth-shemesh and then to Kiriath-jearim (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.6.14","r":"1Sam.6.14","rawR":"1Sam.6.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.6.14","value":"1Sam.6.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.7.1","r":"1Sam.7.1","rawR":"1Sam.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.7.1","value":"1Sam.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:1"},"). When David fled from Saul, he came to Gath and feigned madness before Achish, the king of the city (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.21.10-15","r":"1Sam.21.10-15","rawR":"1Sam.21.10-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.21.10-15","value":"1Sam.21.10-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:10-15"},"). During the rebellion of Absalom, 600 Gittites served among David’s mercenaries (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.15.18","r":"2Sam.15.18","rawR":"2Sam.15.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.15.18","value":"2Sam.15.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 15:18"},"). According to ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.8","r":"2Chr.11.8","rawR":"2Chr.11.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.8","value":"2Chr.11.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 11:8"},", Rehoboam fortified the city of Gath, and ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.12.17","r":"2Kgs.12.17","rawR":"2Kgs.12.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.12.17","value":"2Kgs.12.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kings 12:17"}," relates that it was taken by Hazael, king of Syria, in the ninth century. But it was apparently again in Philistine control when Uzziah broke down its walls (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.26.6","r":"2Chr.26.6","rawR":"2Chr.26.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.26.6","value":"2Chr.26.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 26:6"},"). The city disappeared after being besieged and conquered by Sargon II in the eighth century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Amos.6.2","r":"Amos.6.2","rawR":"Amos.6.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.6.2","value":"Amos.6.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 6:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=PhilistiaPhilistines_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"PhilistiaPhilistines_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"PhilistiaPhilistines_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Philistia, Philistines"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Gath","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Chr 26:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.26.6","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.26.6","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.26.6"},{"anchorText":"Jos 13:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.3","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.3","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 6:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.6.17","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.6.17","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.6.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 18:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.18.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.18.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.18.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 17:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.17.4","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.17.4","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.17.4"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 21:18-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.18-22","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.18-22","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.18-22"},{"anchorText":"Jos 10:36-39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.10.36-39","rawQueryValue":"Josh.10.36-39","sourceRefExact":"Josh.10.36-39"},{"anchorText":"11:21-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.21-22","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.21-22","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.21-22"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 5:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.5.8","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.5.8","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.5.8"},{"anchorText":"6:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.6.14","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.6.14","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.6.14"},{"anchorText":"7:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.7.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.7.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.7.1"},{"anchorText":"21:10-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.21.10-15","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.21.10-15","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.21.10-15"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 15:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.15.18","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.15.18","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.15.18"},{"anchorText":"2 Chronicles 11:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.8","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.8","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.8"},{"anchorText":"2 Kings 12:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.12.17","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.12.17","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.12.17"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 26:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.26.6","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.26.6","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.26.6"},{"anchorText":"Am 6:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.6.2","rawQueryValue":"Amos.6.2","sourceRefExact":"Amos.6.2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c46ce64883c64145d21a2a86f558faffbe941ea354494710133958f44325133c","sourceItemName":"Gath","sourceItemOrder":52,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Gath","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gath","title":"Gath","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}